.TH where 1 "August 2026" "where 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
where \- a fast replacement for the which/where commands on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B where
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B where
helps you locate executables in your system's \fBPATH\fR. It provides features similar to the Windows `where` command, combined with Unix-specific enhancements like symlink resolution, filesystem diagnostics, provenance tracing, and structured JSON outputs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Print all matches (this is the default behavior).
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-first-only
Stop searching after finding the first match.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-show-symlink
Show symlink targets.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-show-size
Show the file size in bytes.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output. Shows permissions, owner, filesystem, and inode details.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Machine-readable output formatted as JSON. Defaults to minified.
.TP
.BR \-\-pretty
Pretty-print the JSON output.
.TP
.BR \-\-yaml
Machine-readable output formatted as YAML.
.TP
.BR \-\-csv
Machine-readable output formatted as CSV.
.TP
.BR \-\-plain
Plain output (paths only, identical to traditional `which`).
.TP
.BR \-\-color
Force colored output even when not attached to a TTY.
.TP
.BR \-\-hash
Compute and display the SHA-256 hash of the matched executables.
.TP
.BR \-\-time
Print the duration it took to complete the search.
.TP
.BR \-\-package
Show the Arch Linux package owner of the binary (uses `pacman -Qo`).
.TP
.BR \-\-version-info
Attempt to extract version information by executing the binary with `--version`.
.TP
.BR \-\-trace
Show command provenance and resolution flow. Details exactly which PATH component was selected and which were shadowed/aliases.
.TP
.BR \-\-benchmark
Show benchmark statistics of the scan (directories searched, entries, elapsed time).
.TP
.BR \-\-doctor
Diagnose PATH issues. Identifies duplicate directory entries, missing paths, dangerous relative paths, and shadowed binaries.
.TP
.BR \-\-generate-completions \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell completions for the specified shell (e.g., bash, zsh, fish).
.TP
.BR \-\-about
Print about information.
.SH CONFIGURATION
You can set default options in \fB~/.config/where/config.toml\fR. 
For example:
.br
  color = true
.br
  output = "json"
.br
  package = true
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success (all commands found, or `--doctor` found no issues).
.TP
.B 1
At least one command was not found, or `--doctor` flagged missing/unreadable directories.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
